{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And I shall set them as your heads.</b> That they should be heads and honored among you, so that you conduct yourselves toward them with awe and honor. And our Rabbis, of blessed memory, interpreted: ״ואשימם בראשיכם״ — ״ואשמם״ is written (without the yod), meaning that the guilt of Israel hangs upon the heads of their judges, for they did not protest against them — even though in our codices it is written with a yod."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:44:35.501238798Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}